---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL('/', Astro.site).toString() },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Download', item: new URL('/download/', Astro.site).toString() },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="Download MacPeek for Mac: Requirements, Install and Verify"
  description="How to get MacPeek: system requirements, the install flow, how to verify the download, and how to build from source while the first signed release is pending."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="wrap narrow article">
    <div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › Download</div>
    <h1>Download MacPeek</h1>
    <p class="lede">Free and open source. Works on Apple silicon and Intel Macs.</p>

    {SITE.hasRelease ? (
      <p><a class="btn primary" href={SITE.releases}>Download the latest release</a> <a class="btn" href={SITE.github}>View source on GitHub</a></p>
    ) : (
      <div class="notice">
        <strong>The first signed release has not been published yet.</strong> Until it is, you can build MacPeek from source (below). When the release is out, this page will link straight to the DMG and its <code>SHA256SUMS</code>. Follow the <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub repository</a> to know when.
      </div>
    )}

    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>macOS 13 (Ventura) or later</li>
      <li>Apple silicon or Intel</li>
      <li>To build from source: full Xcode 15 or later (the standalone Command Line Tools are not enough)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Install a release</h2>
    {SITE.hasRelease ? (
      <Fragment>
        <ol>
          <li>Download <code>MacPeek-x.y.z.dmg</code> from the <a href={SITE.releases}>latest release</a>.</li>
          <li>Open the DMG and drag <strong>MacPeek</strong> to <strong>Applications</strong>.</li>
          <li>Launch MacPeek. The icon appears in your menu bar.</li>
          <li>Open <strong>Manage utilities</strong> to choose what you want.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Releases are built by GitHub Actions, signed with a Developer ID, notarized by Apple and published with a <code>SHA256SUMS</code> file. See <a href="/docs/installation/">verifying the download</a> and the <a href="/security/">security page</a>.</p>
      </Fragment>
    ) : (
      <p>There is nothing to download yet. When the first release is published, this section will walk you through installing it, and releases will come as a signed, notarized DMG with a <code>SHA256SUMS</code> file (see the <a href="/security/">security page</a>). Until then, build from source below.</p>
    )}

    <h2>Build from source</h2>
    <pre><code>git clone {SITE.github}.git
cd MACPeek
sudo xcode-select -s /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer
swift run MacPeek</code></pre>
    <p>More in the <a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>contributing guide</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
